        "title": "Focus Should Be a First-Class Presentation Context",
        "statement": "Twilite should maintain one authoritative focus context, separate from zoom, so the active node or branch can receive richer presentation than the surrounding graph without redefining global zoom semantics.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "plausible",
        "notes": "Zoom establishes the default semantic band. Focus supplies local attention context. A presentation resolver combines the two.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea",
