        "title": "Branch Membership Gets Expensive",
        "description": "If every render must repeatedly traverse graph topology to discover whether each node belongs to the focused branch, focus could make large graphs more expensive to display.",
        "likelihood": "medium",
        "impact": "medium",
        "mitigation": "Keep focus membership derivation centralized and cache or incrementally maintain the focused neighborhood when graph structure or focus changes.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-risk",
        "_classBinding": {
